    <string name="webdav_manual_title">User manual</string>
    <string name="webdav_manual_content">WebDAV sync keeps the current Vault folder consistent across devices while remaining local-first, and provides a controllable remote backup.\n\nSetup:\n1) WebDAV account: enter server URL, username and password, then tap Connect.\n2) Add sync folder pair: set the remote folder path for the current Vault, choose a conflict strategy, and decide whether to sync the database file.\n3) Automation: configure auto sync interval, retry count and retry interval.\n\nCommon scenarios:\n- Phone + tablet: point both devices to the same remote folder.\n- Frequent edits across devices: prefer “Keep both” or “Ask each time” to reduce accidental overwrites.\n\nNotes:\n- First sync can be slow; keep network stable.\n- If conflicts happen, resolve them in the sync task list.\n- Avoid editing the same file offline on multiple devices for long periods.</string>
